<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-PMP YEAR NET FALLS TO A$47.71 MLN.</title>
<headline>RTRS-PMP YEAR NET FALLS TO A$47.71 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    47.71 vs 58.04</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	    10.00 vs 10.00</p>
<p>NOTE: PMP Communications Ltd is a magazine publisher, commercial printer and CD maker. Formerly known as Pacific Magazines and Printing Ltd, PMP was 40 percent owned by News Corp Ltd until early July when News sold its stake.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     20.4 vs 20.4</p>
<p>    Sales				1,096.94 vs 929.96</p>
<p>    Other income			  13.07 vs 3.16</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   19.00 vs 25.80</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		  loss 5.02 vs 6.19 loss</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date Oct 7</p>
<p>Reg date Sept 26</p>
<p>    Tax				     13.64 vs 24.76</p>
<p>    Interest (borrowing costs)	38.87 vs 27.39</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  57.17 vs 44.84</p>
<p>    Minorities			     4.98 vs  1.37</p>
<p>NOTE: PMP said the abnormal loss reflected the write-down in PT Pac-Rim Kwartanusa Printing in Indonesia.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
